{"id": "en_avalanche_p1", "total": 69.61, "segments": [{"text": "If an avalanche catches you on a slope, do not try to outrun the moving snow.", "start": 0.0, "end": 3.14}, {"text": "Jake has less than 15 minutes to survive when the mountain slope suddenly breaks apart.", "start": 4.16, "end": 7.8}, {"text": "A massive slab of heavy snow crashes down the peak, rushing straight toward his shelter.", "start": 8.34, "end": 12.16}, {"text": "One. Try to get off the sliding slab to the side as it starts moving.", "start": 12.74, "end": 16.14}, {"text": "Jake scrambles toward a rock overhang, but the fast white wave sweeps him away.", "start": 17.26, "end": 20.68}, {"text": "Two. If you are swept away, fight with swimming motions to stay on top.", "start": 21.34, "end": 24.7}, {"text": "He swims against the crushing current and dumps his heavy pack to avoid sinking down.", "start": 25.4, "end": 28.6}, {"text": "Three. As the snow slows, cup your arm in front of your face quickly.", "start": 29.32, "end": 32.46}, {"text": "Jake crouches down beneath the rock overhang and creates a crucial air pocket around his face.", "start": 33.36, "end": 37.04}, {"text": "He pushes one hand up toward the surface right as the debris comes to a stop.", "start": 37.64, "end": 40.64}, {"text": "Jake waves his bare hand through the top crust to show rescuers where he is buried.", "start": 41.46, "end": 45.22}, {"text": "Most buried people need to be dug out within about 15 minutes to stay alive.", "start": 46.06, "end": 49.48}, {"text": "Essential rescue gear like a beacon, probe, and shovel can save a life in time.", "start": 50.24, "end": 54.1}, {"text": "Jake secured his breathing space and marked his exact location for his waiting climbing partner.", "start": 54.9, "end": 58.74}, {"text": "It was the perfect plan for survival. There was just one major problem left.", "start": 59.22, "end": 62.66}, {"text": "The heavy snow is packing tight, and his partner has no shovel to dig him out.", 